\section{Reading the Output}{

Every estimation and testing function returns a tidy \code{data.frame}
with a \code{term} column and a numeric \code{value} column, carrying the
\code{poemed_tbl} class so it prints with whole numbers shown without a
decimal part, other quantities to a few significant figures, and
p-values to four decimal places. The stored numbers keep full
precision; only the display rounds. See \link{poemed_tbl} for the details.
}

\section{How to Cite}{

If you use POEMED in published work, please cite Yu and Kelley (in
press), the article that introduces its methods and the package.
\code{citation("POEMED")} gives the full reference and a BibTeX entry.
}

